    "result_text": "All tests green (3/3, `BUILD SUCCESS`). The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`; the other two files are support code.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded optional owner `email` \u2014 stored and returned lower-cased, rejected with 400 when present but syntactically invalid. I kept structural impact low by adding a small, cohesive step + escalation rather than growing any existing class, and never modified an existing function body.\n\n**New small units (each ~one trivial method, no surrounding complexity):**\n- `NormalizeOwnerEmail.java` \u2014 POST-pipeline step: skips a missing email, lower-cases a valid one in place, throws on an invalid one.\n- `InvalidOwnerEmailException.java` + `InvalidOwnerEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 dedicated checked exception \u2192 400, matching the codebase's existing per-concern escalation pattern (e.g. `DuplicateTelephoneException`).\n- Escalation YAML wiring the exception to its handler.\n\n**Minimal edits to existing files (no existing function changed):**\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added the `email` field + plain accessors (new methods only; no existing method touched).\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the optional `email` property (`format: email`) to `OwnerFields`, so the generated DTOs expose it and MapStruct maps it in both directions automatically (no mapper change needed).\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `normalizeEmail` step into the pipeline.\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `email` column; `data.sql` \u2014 extended the positional seed inserts to match.\n\n**Scope note:** the spec and tests cover create + read-back. The PUT/update path was intentionally left untouched to avoid growing `ApplyOwner`; email is not currently editable via PUT. Let me know if you'd like update support too.",
